# Rebuild after changes

After any change to `source/`, `tests/`, `assets/`, `CMakeLists.txt`, or plugin-related CMake, **rebuild every shipping format** and report success or errors. Do not ask the user to rebuild manually unless the toolchain is broken.

The editor is native JUCE (`source/ui/`). There is no web frontend, npm build, dev server, or embedded UI bundle.

## Required build (always)

**Do not** build only `MidiPhrases_Standalone`. Standalone and DAW plugins are separate binaries; a standalone-only build leaves VST3/AU stale.

**Always** run the full default build:

```bash
cmake --build Builds
```

That rebuilds **Standalone**, **AU**, **VST3**, and **AUv3**, and copies AU/VST3 to `~/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/` via `COPY_PLUGIN_AFTER_BUILD`.

Equivalent explicit targets (only if you truly need a subset — prefer full build):

```bash
cmake --build Builds --target MidiPhrases_Standalone MidiPhrases_VST3 MidiPhrases_AU MidiPhrases_AUv3
```

Built standalone (Debug):

`Builds/MidiPhrases_artefacts/Debug/Standalone/MIDI Phrases.app`

Remind the user to **fully quit and reopen** the standalone after a rebuild. An already-running instance keeps the old binary.

## Plugin C++ (`source/`), CMake, tests

1. If `CMakeLists.txt` or the embedded font list changed: `cmake -B Builds -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug`
2. **Always:** `cmake --build Builds` (all formats above)
3. Run `./Builds/Tests` when test or processor behavior changes.

## DAW reload

After plugin binaries change, tell the user to **remove the plugin instance and reopen it** (or restart the DAW). Rescan plug-in folders only when the host does not pick up replaced bundles automatically.
